2.2 Statistical Analysis
First, we used standard descriptive analyses to gain an initial understanding of the dataset. This included heat maps of each measured street segment that showed the median percentage of cars above the speed limit by weekday and time of day. To analyse the spatial predictor variables, we calculated the total ratio of speeding for each segment, i.e. the sum of cars driving above the speed limit during the whole study period divided by the total number of cars during the whole study period. Since the outcome variable is a ratio, we used Bayesian beta regression models. To analyse the temporal and spatio—temporal variables, we will test zero one inflated beta models [18] and ordered beta regression models [19], as segments can have hourly speeding ratios of 0 or 1. These analyses are very processing intensive and are still ongoing at the time of writing this paper. All statistical analyses were carried out in in R v4.3.1 [20] and Stan v2.26.1 [21].


